☐ failure to validate a patient-reported outcome questionnaire;
☐ the placement of a clinical hold on a study;
☐ the failure of third parties conducting and overseeing the operations of our clinical trials to perform their contractual or regulatory
obligations in a timely fashion;
☐ exposure of clinical trial subjects to unexpected and unacceptable health risks or noncompliance with regulatory requirements, which may
result in suspension of the trial; and
☐ manufacturing and/or distribution issues associated with clinical supplies.
Completion of clinical trials for each product candidate will be required before commercialization. If Endo or we experience delays in, or termination of,
clinical trials, or fails to enroll patients in clinical trials in a timely manner, or if the cost or timing of the regulatory approval process increases, our financial
results and the commercial prospects for product candidates for new indications will be adversely impacted.
